# This project needs its devDependencies (typescript, vitest, prisma, eslint,
# prettier, ...) for every install — including `npm ci` in CI. Some developer
# machines / environments inject a default of `omit=dev`, which would silently
# drop the whole toolchain. `omit=` (empty) here overrides that at the project
# level so `npm install`/`npm ci` behavior is identical for everyone.
#
# Note: npm prints a cosmetic "invalid config omit=\"\"" warning for the empty
# value, but honors it (empty omit = omit nothing). This is preferable to a
# silent, machine-dependent install that omits dev dependencies.
omit=
